From: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
Subject: ath10k-ct: demote unsupported pdev param log

CT firmware can legitimately lack some pdev parameters used by common
ath10k setup paths.  The command still returns -EOPNOTSUPP, but printing a
warning for WMI_PDEV_PARAM_UNSUPPORTED during normal operation is noisy on
devices where wireless continues to work.

--- a/ath10k-6.18/wmi.c
+++ b/ath10k-6.18/wmi.c
@@ -7261,8 +7261,8 @@ ath10k_wmi_op_gen_pdev_set_param(struct
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
 
 	if (id == WMI_PDEV_PARAM_UNSUPPORTED) {
-		ath10k_warn(ar, "pdev param %d not supported by firmware\n",
-			    id);
+		ath10k_dbg(ar, ATH10K_DBG_WMI,
+			   "pdev param %d not supported by firmware\n", id);
 		return ERR_PTR(-EOPNOTSUPP);
 	}
 
